# Real production paperwork (Never commit raw confidential assets).
# Third-party call sheets, camera reports and script logs are copyrighted and
# routinely carry crew personal data, so they stay out of the repository.
# Point CINESPINE_EXAMPLES_DIR at a local copy instead.
data/raw/
data/staging/
data/examples/
*.pdf
*.cif
*.kdm
*.db
spine.db
# WAL mode keeps two sidecar files beside the database. They hold committed
# data that has not been checkpointed yet, so they are as local as the db.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local code-intelligence indexes (rebuilt on demand, machine-specific)
.codegraph/
graphify-out/
